<figure class="system-map system-map-memory" aria-labelledby="memory-map-title">
  <figcaption id="memory-map-title">
    <span class="map-kicker">Retrieval architecture</span>
    <strong>Exact words and related meaning meet in one ranking</strong>
    <span>The pipeline keeps useful context while removing repeated or stale results.</span>
  </figcaption>

  <div class="memory-query"><span>Question</span><strong>What did we decide, and why?</strong></div>

  <div class="memory-retrievers" role="list">
    <section class="map-node" role="listitem">
      <span class="map-index">LEXICAL</span>
      <strong>FTS5 with BM25</strong>
      <p>Finds exact names, commands, phrases, and file references.</p>
      <small>Top 30 candidates</small>
    </section>
    <section class="map-node" role="listitem">
      <span class="map-index">SEMANTIC</span>
      <strong>Exact cosine search</strong>
      <p>Finds related decisions even when the question uses different words.</p>
      <small>sqlite vec · top 30 candidates</small>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="memory-ranking" role="list">
    <span role="listitem"><strong>RRF</strong> merges both rankings</span>
    <span role="listitem"><strong>MMR</strong> reduces repetition</span>
    <span role="listitem"><strong>Decay</strong> weighs type and freshness</span>
    <span role="listitem"><strong>Result</strong> returns five memories</span>
  </div>

  <div class="memory-stores">
    <div><span>Curated Brain</span><strong>Rules · facts · decisions</strong></div>
    <div><span>Echo archive</span><strong>Original transcript chunks</strong></div>
  </div>
</figure>
